#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Lessons as design rules"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Each rule below comes from a failure that happened while running this architecture with real data, stated in its general form. They are the reasons behind many of the [principles]{1} and contract clauses; when a rule looks over-cautious, it is because its absence once cost something."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Measuring and verifying"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Tuning and measurement harnesses call the real production code path. A missing required input raises; it never falls back silently."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Calibrate a detector's positive class on independent real-world captures (different devices, damaged copies), not on clean re-renders of the same source."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "A processing chain encodes assumptions about its target. Re-validate every stage when re-aiming it, because deleted signal and absent signal look the same downstream."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "No mitigation counts as done until a measurement on representative data shows its effect."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "\"Deployed\" is a claim about the running process. Verify it by asking the live system for a marker only the new version emits."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Check the artefact itself (deployed state, filled tables), never a status line or a cached plan."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "A configuration the schema accepts is not proof of behaviour. Read the deployed object back to confirm it, and delete inert configuration that looks authoritative."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Idempotency, delivery and concurrency"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Deduplicate at two independent layers: the orchestrator rejects a duplicate run identifier, and the work short-circuits on terminal state."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Write to a temporary location and move into place atomically, so a replay never sees a half-finished output."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Human decisions outrank redeliveries in upsert guards. Guards test the condition that makes an operation wrong, not a status label."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Test every migration on a database it has already been applied to; \"idempotent\" is a claim about the second run. Never cache schema facts indefinitely."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Enforce mutual exclusion in the database: a unique key, and select and acquire in one statement. Check the lease before the first write."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Judge health from a heartbeat, not from process statistics. Isolate per-item failures (quarantine and continue) so one poisoned input cannot wedge the pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Chain stages by hand-off so fallback paths are unreachable. A job's timeout is at least the sum of its tasks' budgets."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Each statement against a transactional table format is a commit. Batch into set-based operations and keep tail work at a constant number of round trips."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Stores and data of record"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Before anything empties a store, establish whether it is the source of record. Archive successes, dead-letter rejects with a reason, and derive locations from content hashes."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Keep one manifest of what a secondary store carries, derive sync and lag checks from it, and test that every reporting source has a writer."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Reconcile primary and secondary stores. A job's success says nothing about a write it made after its own commit."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Never deploy from an uncommitted tree. Alert on data freshness, not only on job failure."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Validate references against the authoritative registry with a foreign key. Constrain bad history going forward rather than rewriting it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Identity, grants and infrastructure as code"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "A declarative permission block is the complete set: it revokes whatever it does not list. Confirm a hypothesis with read-only queries against the live system before acting on it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "An identity is not configuration. Recreating a resource can mint a new principal, so parameterise principals and keep code that verifies every layer of grants."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Version privileges alongside the schema, including default privileges for objects that future migrations create."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Size a deploy identity for what it must create, make it the owner of what it deploys, and copy deployment state rather than file trees."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Check privileges before the first run under a new identity. A right to manage without a right to create is a drop with no undo."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Declare an explicit dependency between a permission and its first use. One green apply may have been lucky ordering."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Plan and apply share their state and path parameters from one definition. Run the first apply where failure is cheap."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Scope credentials to the single step that needs them."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Render environment-specific artefacts from the deployment tool's resolved output, and expose on a health endpoint the environment each service believes it is in."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Data protection and provenance"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Prove provenance per object before any destructive drop. A schema or a repository is not a unit of provenance."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Write exclusion rules by kind of data (spreadsheets, exported learner lists), not by remembered file names."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Normalise external identities once, at the boundary, and enforce the normal form with a constraint."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Failure signalling"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Make missing data loud (strict undefined) and pin the strictness with a test."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Keep \"refused bad input\" and \"system broken\" in separate counters and statuses."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "A tolerated failure matches and names the specific error it tolerates."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Every path that produces a stored derived value calls one implementation, and fallback paths are exercised by tests."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Every recurring job has a seconds-long \"nothing to do\" exit on the cheapest compute. Automation never starts paid compute without consent."
msgstr ""
